course: dictionary
lesson: 5094
title: Interact
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To interact means to do things with other people, or with things, and to respond to them. You can interact by talking, playing or working together. In a team game, you interact with your teammates when you pass the ball and answer them.
explain: Things can also interact when they affect each other. «Some medicines interact, making each other stronger or weaker.» The medicines are not just sitting side by side. They change each other, so interact here means affect each other.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. Who or what is doing the interacting? Is it people, things, or a computer? «Natural does not mean safe: some herbal remedies can harm, or interact with other medicines.» The words harm and medicines tell you this is about things that affect each other, not people chatting.
fact: To interact means to talk, play or work with other people and respond to them.
fact: In science, things interact when they affect each other, like chemicals or animals in a food web.
fact: To interact with a computer, game or screen means to use it by clicking, touching or speaking.
fact: Interaction is the noun, and interactive is the adjective: an interactive whiteboard responds when you touch it.
fact: «Some medicines interact», so doctors and pharmacists need to know about every medicine and herbal remedy a person takes.
exercise: «Some medicines interact, making each other stronger or weaker.» What does interact mean here? | Get rid of each other | Sit quietly side by side | Run away from each other | *Affect each other
exercise: Mia wants to ___ with her classmates in group work. Which word fits best? | interrupt | intercept | *interact | interest
exercise: What does it mean to interact with a touchscreen? | To break it by pressing too hard | *To use it by touching, clicking or speaking | To look at it without touching it | To switch it off for the night
test: In a food web, what does it mean when animals interact? | They all sleep at the same time | *They affect each other, for example by eating each other | They never see each other | They change into plants
test: Which word means able to respond to touch or clicks? | *interactive | interaction | interrupted | interacted
exam: A doctor warns, «Do not take these pills together, they may interact.» What does the doctor mean? | *They may affect each other, making each other stronger or weaker | They should be eaten with bread | They are two different colours | They have no effect on each other at all
